From: Ashley <ashley@shuuri.net>
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: qcom-ipcc: mask the IRQ across system suspend

The ADSP charger firmware pushes BATTMGR_NOTIFICATION over pmic_glink
while the system sleeps. Each one rings the IPCC mailbox IRQ, which is
requested with IRQF_NO_SUSPEND and so is never masked, and pulls the SoC
back out of suspend every few minutes.

Drop IRQF_NO_SUSPEND so the IRQ is masked during suspend like any other.
Co-processor doorbells no longer wake the AP; pending signals are
handled on resume.

Verified by its author on the Retroid Pocket 6: 30+ minute uninterrupted
sleeps where the device could not stay asleep past 5 to 10 minutes.

[ ROCKNIX SM8550 0502 and SM8750 0504, same one-line change ]
---
 drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
@@ -326,8 +326,7 @@
 		goto err_mbox;
 
 	ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, ipcc->irq, qcom_ipcc_irq_fn,
-			       IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH | IRQF_NO_SUSPEND |
-			       IRQF_NO_THREAD, name, ipcc);
+			       IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH | IRQF_NO_THREAD, name, ipcc);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err_req_irq;
 
